{
  "id": "news_trend",
  "version": 1,
  "title": "News and technical trend",
  "description": "Long one contract when MACD 12/26/9 crosses above its signal line while the close is above its 200-session average and the news is positive: the mean sentiment of the stories published in the last 3 days, as a model rated them. Flat when MACD crosses below its signal line, whatever the news.",
  "required_bar": "1D",
  "conditions": [
    "Trend and momentum: it buys a MACD cross-above only in an uptrend (close above SMA 200), and only when the recent news agrees.",
    "News sentiment is read only as it could have been known: each story counts from its publication plus a declared 5-minute processing latency, and only stories published in the 3 days before a close count there. Each story counts once, in its latest version by then; later copies of a story's text from other outlets are dropped.",
    "Missing or stale sentiment (no rated story in the last 3 days) blocks new entries. Exits do not depend on the news: a MACD cross-below always exits.",
    "Sentiment comes from a model's rating of each story, recorded once and replayed. Ratings recorded after the stories could have been used are exploratory evidence on real news; the fixture's stories are invented, so its runs are synthetic.",
    "Long or flat only; it never sells short.",
    "Daily bars. Signals are decided at the close and filled at the next session's open, with the backtest's commission and slippage."
  ],
